{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/958881-a-good-system-for-armour-weapons","id":958881,"title":"A good system for Armour/weapons","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-27T14:03:53-07:00","id":958881,"title":"A good system for Armour/weapons","content":"So, it pains me, but combat in world of darkness is really only good if your characters are changing breeds and your players know how a fight works. Sadly, most of the gamelines don't involve playing savage naked beasts and your average player doesn't know what a punch is. This problem is further confounded when the developers make stupid mistakes like thinking a warhammer is a bashing blunt weapon, (or in other games, a greatsword is difficulty 5, Strength+6) and a bigger problem, far bigger, is that some armours are -3 dexterity, meaning you need Olympian levels of fitness to wear it, because armour is apparently not supposed to be a practical form of protection.<br /> <br /> Weapons and armour are used by people, and should be ballanced for people/what they would be in real life, to the nearest approximate that mechanics can get to without bogging down. -3 dex for armour... well, that's just unfeasible for humans.<br /> <br /> My friend told me that -3 dexterity is fine cause it's for vampires and they can blood buff and have physical disciplines, and that the example knight in the book had 4 in dex (and 4 in most attributes) so it's ok, but he's the stupidest friend I have, so I won't listen to him. (no seriously, the average professional soldier will have 2-3 dex. You don't make common soldiers Olympians, nor should you drastically different rules to them)Mage 20 is better than most, I think. I use it for other splats. Well, it's not 'good' It just isn't all bad. Sure there's some odd things up there (leather dusters are as limiting as plate? Sure.) But let's try to avoid the claymores and the warhammers and the dusters and punch daggers (and most certainly avoid the Flak jackets and 11th century broadsword) It's more the system than the things in it.<br /> Armour is by far worse than weapons. A simplistic &quot;+soak, -dex&quot; system. Melee Guns are mostly alright. Melee weapons fall apart with reach.<br /> <br /> <br /> I liked that mage, for weapons, had little numbered notes on. Like Special #7- +1 to opponent's block attempts. Keep that. Do that more.<br /> <br /> ARMOUR<br /> Should be at different difficulties to avoid. A breastplate/vest is at +1 difficulty, while a guy in full plate might be at +3 or +4.<br /> Should be more effective at negating certain types of damage. A sword slash might have an increased difficulty to do damage against medieval mail, and might do bashing rather than lethal(or aggravated!) if less than the armour value is scored in damage.<br /> <br /> More reasonable penalties for armour use than Dexterity penalties include<br /> Penalties to initiative.<br /> +1 or 2 difficulty to athletics rolls. This might double in some situations (like swimming)<br /> Cost and conceal. Armour, Modern or old is expensive and is a massive sign that you're planning to be in a fight. You could hide a vest under a suit, but you can't hide the thicker military stuff under something so thin.<br /> <br /> I liked that mage, for weapons, had little numbered notes on. Like for a weapon there was Special #7- &quot;+1 to opponent's block attempts&quot;. Keep that. Do it for armour.<br /> <br /> Examples of armour.<br /> Light 'soft' kevlar vest. 3 armour, +0 on athletics rolls. Jacket conceal. -1 initiative. +1 to avoid (vest). +0 to any damage.<br /> Mail hauberk. 3 armour. +1 on athletic rolls. Coat conceal. -2 initiative, +2 to avoid. +1 to cutting<br /> Plate. 5 armour. +2 on athletics. No conceal. -4 initiative. +4 to avoid. +1 to cutting and +1 concussive<br /> Full Modern military . 5 armour. +1 on athletics. No conceal, -2 initiative. +2 avoid. +1 to projectiles<br /> <br /> <br /> Totally a crude thing by me. Would work much better laid out in a table. The strengths weaknesses of an armour might get simplified to a few words, or something done in the weapon section.<br /> Just a stupid example of how this works.<br /> <i>Sam tries to cut alex with a sword. Alex is wearing Mail. Mail is resistant against cutting, so sam rolls damage at difficulty 7 rather than 6. Sam gets two successes, but the armour value of Mail is 3, so the blade never hit skin, and the damage is bashing. Alex can soak with both armour and stamina. </i><br /> Next action<br /> <i>Sam tries again. This time stabbing Alex. Mail isn't extra special against stabbing, so the difficulty is 6 rather than 7. Sam gets 5 successes on the damage roll, breaching the 3 armour. The damage is lethal, which Alex can't soak meaning only the armour can reduce the damage. Alex rolls Armour to soak</i><br /> <br /> <br /> Melee<br /> <br /> Fighting a longer weapon means -1 dice and -2 initiative. Fighting a much longer weapon means -2 dice and -4 initiative.<br /> Fighting in an enclosed space with a weapon that's too long can result in +1 or even +2 difficulty.<br /> Small weapons are +2 to parry with. Heavy weapons are +1.<br /> <br /> Characters can use a dodge at +2 difficulty to get past a reach weapon and have reach weapon rules turned around. The reach weapon user can dodge-backup for +1 to counter this.<br /> Precision hold. Character's grip is further up the weapon for stabbing weapons (Halfswording, spears). Meaning they loose all advantage of reach, but reduce the difficulty to hit precisely and gain +2 armour penetration.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Range.<br /> Caryover is limited to the weapon's damage. a man with 7 successes on a light pistol (4) does a max of 8 dice of damage.<br /> Weapons have different recoil. One gun might be +0 burst fire and +2 full auto. Another might be +2 burst fire and +3 full auto.<br /> Shotguns (firing shells) are -1 difficulty to hit, but are +1 to do damage for any form of armour.<br /> Big guns, like high powered sniper /anti material rifles (or anything that'll do more than 8 damage a shot), are +1 difficulty (or more) to use.<br /> <br /> <br /> Or, well, this is at least my rough attempt. Part of me is wanting to simplify it a bit more, another part says it sounds more complex here than it would in a book because I'm rather bad with explaining.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7244-innocent-flower","name":"Innocent Flower","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7244_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T15:33:06-07:00","id":958920,"title":"","content":"If you're going to overhaul WoD armors and weapons?<br /> <br /> Take a page from Exalted 3e and throw &quot;realism&quot; out the window as a concern. The WoD combat system doesn't work well for weapon-porn lists upon lists of weapons, mod kits, and so on to fine-tune every equipment choice. Have three basic kinds of each general class of weapon (hand-to-hand, thrown, archery, firearms), and for armors: a light version with the least potency but the least penalties, a balanced medium, and a heavy version.<br /> <br /> Then just write up 'tags' as needed to differentiate weapons and armors.<br /> <br /> It's faster, it's easier, you can make new weapon/armor stats with ease because you select one of three base stats and apply tags.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T16:25:59-07:00","id":958945,"title":"","content":"No, I disagree. If you want a more effective combat system, look at Shadowrun 4e. It is cinematic, but it works well for fast combat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T17:55:01-07:00","id":958981,"title":"","content":"I like the approach that <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7244-innocent-flower\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7244_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7244\" data-vbnamecard=\"7244\">Innocent Flower</a> proposes. As long as it can be limited to a page or so, I would give it a try. I think so far this seems like a decent balance between simplistic and complex. I have wished the armor system was better. I never really agreed with the whole Dex penalty balance.<br /> <br /> Never played Exalted, so I don't know anything about this tag system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T19:11:07-07:00","id":959021,"title":"","content":"The Ex3 tag system isn't that different from what was proposed, but you can write it out with words (though they well translate into standard mechanical widgets).<br /> <br /> So, you'd get things like this:<br /> <br /> Brass Knuckles - Light Hand-to-Hand Weapon. Tags: Bashing, Brawl, Worn. Resources 1.<br /> Knife - Light Hand-to-Hand Weapon. Tags: Lethal, Melee, <i>optional</i> Thrown (Short). Resources N/A.<br /> One Handed Sword - Medium Hand-to-Hand Weapon. Tags: Lethal, Melee, Balanced. Resources 2.<br /> Lance/Heavy Spear - Heavy Hand-to-Hand Weapon. Tags: Lethal, Melee, Piercing, Reaching, Two-Handed (if on foot). Resources 1.<br /> <br /> Obviously the specific mechanics are a bit meaningless if you don't know Exalted, but I think it gets the idea across of how it works out and most of the tags are self-explanatory in intent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T20:02:38-07:00","id":959040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/958881-a-good-system-for-armour-weapons?p=959021#post959021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Ex3 tag system isn't that different from what was proposed, but you can write it out with words (though they well translate into standard mechanical widgets).<br /> <br /> So, you'd get things like this:<br /> <br /> Brass Knuckles - Light Hand-to-Hand Weapon. Tags: Bashing, Brawl, Worn. Resources 1.<br /> Knife - Light Hand-to-Hand Weapon. Tags: Lethal, Melee, <i>optional</i> Thrown (Short). Resources N/A.<br /> One Handed Sword - Medium Hand-to-Hand Weapon. Tags: Lethal, Melee, Balanced. Resources 2.<br /> Lance/Heavy Spear - Heavy Hand-to-Hand Weapon. Tags: Lethal, Melee, Piercing, Reaching, Two-Handed (if on foot). Resources 1.<br /> <br /> Obviously the specific mechanics are a bit meaningless if you don't know Exalted, but I think it gets the idea across of how it works out and most of the tags are self-explanatory in intent.</div> </div> </div> </div>So there is a general chat with all of these weapons and then a page or two of tags with explanations? That could work just as well. Not terribly different from what was proposed","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T20:35:13-07:00","id":959052,"title":"","content":"It's not, but the big difference is that it cuts down on variables if you're making something that's not in the examples provided. Instead of, &quot;one a scale of 1-5, what armor rating should this have?&quot; and then have to decide, &quot;should this be a +1 penalty to athletics, or a +2 to athletics?&quot; You're applying pre-built components together.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T20:48:06-07:00","id":959060,"title":"","content":"How would you handle Ancient vs Modern Armors, or would they both end up on the same chart? I could see an argument for having 2 different sets, given the vast differences between the 2. Or at its base, Full Riot Gear and Full Plate (I know, only used for a very small window of time) are effectively the same, just with different tags?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T23:17:37-07:00","id":959117,"title":"","content":"Same with different tags. The Ex3 example falls down a bit here (armor tags in Ex3 are sorely lacking), but modern riot and military combat armors would have access to something like a Flexible tag to represent the more forgiving and lighter weight materials available, as well there would need to be some sort of Proofed (Category) tag that modern armors would have focused on bullets and light hand-to-hand weapons (for anti-stab plates), where things like plate mail would be tagged against edged weapons and archery.<br /> <br /> Resource cost would also be a major factor in a current day game, since functional archaic armor is going to be much more expensive to get and maintain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T00:20:08-07:00","id":959132,"title":"","content":"Regarding armor, ( Shameless Plug incoming! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ), also peek at <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/600305-alternative-armor-system\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-armor-system</a><br /> While I don't really handle different avoidance ratings and effectiveness against different kinds of attacks, I splitted armor up into different kinds of armor, <i>based on how they mitigate or absorb damage</i>. I didn't want to make things too complex with numbers.<br /> <br /> Pershaps you'll find something that strikes your fancy for your rewrite. Feel free to re-use anything in there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T01:19:10-07:00","id":959144,"title":"","content":"I have written a building-block system for weapons and armors in the WoD some time back, that would allow for a great variety of different armament while keeping it all balanced.<br /> Suffice to say it was a ton of work.<br /> If anyone is interested just PM me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6112-seki","name":"Seki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T07:14:53-07:00","id":959227,"title":"","content":"I would suggest, at the very least, allowing ballistic weapons, like modern firearms, to ignore any armor that does not have a ballistic tag (chain mail would not but Kevlar would). Heck, to make combat more believable, I have firearms ignore any form of natural soak, even supernatural soak, and any form of non-ballistic armor. In addition, I inflict armor penalties only when the bonuses for armor exceed the sum of Strength and Stamina of a character (one die of penalties for every level of above Strength plus Stamina).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T09:08:36-07:00","id":959291,"title":"","content":"Chain would prptect against bullets, the thing is that most guns do more than 3 damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7244-innocent-flower","name":"Innocent Flower","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7244_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T09:39:25-07:00","id":959306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/958881-a-good-system-for-armour-weapons?p=959227#post959227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Heck, to make combat more believable, I have firearms ignore any form of natural soak, even supernatural soak, and any form of non-ballistic armor.</div> </div> </div> </div>How does it make any sense that &quot;supernatural soak&quot; doesn't work against bullets?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T12:49:04-07:00","id":959378,"title":"","content":"Because high velocity rounds did not exist when those powers evolved over ten thousand years ago?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T13:57:12-07:00","id":959443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/958881-a-good-system-for-armour-weapons?p=959378#post959378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because high velocity rounds did not exist when those powers evolved over ten thousand years ago?</div> </div> </div> </div>So a Fera or Vampire with Fortitude could attempt to soak lava, but not a .22? Same with crossbow bolts, lightning, terminal velocity falls. Why should bullets be treated like some magic form of damage that is unsoakable?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T15:28:07-07:00","id":959521,"title":"","content":"And for armour... well, it's basic physics. Chainmail would slow down anything penetrating it, unless it was huge. A lead bullet, steel arrow head and a railgun round will all eventually be stopped by materials. The difference isn't &quot;well, this armour doesn't work&quot; the technology instead says &quot;well, this is a lot more dice and an AP value&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7244-innocent-flower","name":"Innocent Flower","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7244_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T16:28:15-07:00","id":959560,"title":"","content":"Well, there is nothing in natural that is a dense projectile that exceeds the speed of sound, so no one would have experimented against that threat when developing supernatural toughness. As for chainmail, you would be better off wearing a cotton t-shirt, the bullet is unlikely to pull the t-shirt into the wound, but it will likely pull the chainmail into the wound. Anyway, metal armor is almost never think enough to stop bullets, a centimeter of hardened steel might stop a modern heavy pistol round (a Ruger Super Warhawk, .454 Casull), but it would not stop a modern medium rifle round (a FN BAR Magnum, .300 WM), and it would weigh around 160 kilograms. Armor piercing rounds are even more effective against body armor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T18:36:06-07:00","id":959606,"title":"","content":"Why are we assuming that supernatural powers are the result of experimentation by prehistoric supernaturals, and only against natural phenomena?<br /> <br /> Why would a mage only worry about magic protection spells that can defend against &quot;slow&quot; things like an arrow, when mages can make an arrow fly as fast as a modern bullet, or hit you with a lightning bolt (which moves much faster than sound)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T21:53:01-07:00","id":959664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/958881-a-good-system-for-armour-weapons?p=959560#post959560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, there is nothing in natural that is a dense projectile that exceeds the speed of sound, so no one would have experimented against that threat when developing supernatural toughness.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think Supernatural toughness is the result of having experimented. It just is. You don't need to test Fortitude or Fera soak against something (in this case, bullets), and evolve your soak pool over time, against said damage. Some Elders can take a train to the face and be okay (looking at the Marble Flesh, Fortitude Gangrel). They don't have to experiment with train kissing to have that soak pool.<br /> I mean, in the end, this discussion doesn't even matter because for your table, you've chosen bullets to be unsoakable damage. Whatever works for you, but that really doesn't make any sense from an in game perspective or an out of game one. <br /> And I keep putting Fera soak and Fortitude together, because they generally soak all non bane damage the same.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T06:30:10-07:00","id":959780,"title":"","content":"So in middle age you could use fortitude to soak a spear thrown at mach speed by n elder with potence 7 celerity 7 but today you can't soak a bullet?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T07:26:04-07:00","id":959798,"title":"","content":"Regarding Armor Penalty:<br /> I've been using a houserule that removes penaltypoints depending on how good a fighter you are. Each dot in Melee/Brawl/Archery/Firearms removes one point of penalty. That means that a Swordsman with Melee 3 has learned to fight in a full plate armor and therefore don't get penalties from it. While a novice haven't learned to compensate and therefore still has penalties.<br /> <br /> But i agree that the whole combat system in all WoD gamelines needs an overhaul. It simply takes to much time (especially with Celerity, Rage etc), gets confusing etc.<br /> The best thing would boil it all down to one opposed roll (Attack+Strength vs Evade/Soak) but i haven't figured out a good way to incorporate a persons strength, dexterity, toughness, armor, weapon damage etc into these two rolls.<br /> I don't mind multiple actions (since i think that much more that a punch and a block can be accomplished in a 3 second timespan), but to me they complicate things.<br /> Another thing that's been bothering me is that if someone throws a punch or attempt to stab you etc, you will attempt to block/evade this. Doing other things that evading damage should be a dedicated action that needs a Willpower roll or a Willpower point spend to follow through with IMO.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/ghw20supporterhiddengaroup\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/n18segp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0v25ewp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">English is not my native language, so i apologize for errors in grammar or spelling.</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/392-cadmiumcadamium","name":"Cadmiumcadamium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar392_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"936"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T07:35:22-07:00","id":959805,"title":"","content":"I also think that, well, having great strength should allow you an easier time in armour. No 'Well you get dex from celerity and that cancels out the dex penality' but, well. Strength should, but not completely, migitate the problems of having excess weight. Potence, whatever mages use, and maybe glabro if you find something fitting should all reduce penalties (with some hard armour keeping at least some penalty because of how rigid and in the way it is, rather than weight)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7244-innocent-flower","name":"Innocent Flower","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7244_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T08:02:44-07:00","id":959818,"title":"","content":"Maybe something like &quot;a character does not suffer from penalties if his Strength or related combat ability rating is greater that the penalty&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/ghw20supporterhiddengaroup\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/n18segp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0v25ewp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">English is not my native language, so i apologize for errors in grammar or spelling.</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/392-cadmiumcadamium","name":"Cadmiumcadamium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar392_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"936"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T08:13:48-07:00","id":959822,"title":"","content":"Anyway, i managed to boil down what traits are necessary in a fight.<br /> <b>Attack</b> (used for):<br /> Dexterity (Accuracy, Initiative)<br /> Strength (Power)<br /> Wits (Initiative)<br /> Brawl/Melee (Accuracy)<br /> Weapon Damage (Power)<br /> Celerity (Accuracy)<br /> Potence (Power)<br /> <br /> <b>Defence </b>(used for):<br /> Dexterity (Avoidance, Initiative)<br /> Stamina (Toughness)<br /> Wits (Initiative)<br /> Athletics (Avoidance)<br /> Armor Rating (Toughness)<br /> Celerity (Avoidance)<br /> Fortitude (Toughness).<br /> <br /> What if someone can somehow build an Attack vs Defence opposed roll from these traits...I had some though of just combining all related traits into one pool and then split it in two but that doesn't seem to work out well. I know that i included Disciplines in this (mostly because i am a Vampire player primarily).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/ghw20supporterhiddengaroup\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/n18segp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0v25ewp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">English is not my native language, so i apologize for errors in grammar or spelling.</span></span>","edited":{"userid":392,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/392-cadmiumcadamium","user":"Cadmiumcadamium","date":". 08-29-2016, 11:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/392-cadmiumcadamium","name":"Cadmiumcadamium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar392_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"936"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T08:50:00-07:00","id":959845,"title":"","content":"Kinda wish for more variables with that though. <br /> For example, potence can be used to leap out of danger. It could also be used to put a heavy defensive item between you.<br /> Also, Intimidation and misdirection are great things in fights. <br /> <br /> Mage has this quick roll thing for going over an entire fight. It's Your favourite combat attribute and your favourite fight skill VS theirs. If you want simplification, go for that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7244-innocent-flower","name":"Innocent Flower","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7244_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T11:24:59-07:00","id":959918,"title":"","content":"Okay, just a word of advice here..<br /> While Alternate System building can be utterly fun, it's easy to lose track of something important:<br /> <br /> Keep It Simple for the players.<br /> <br /> You don't want them to row through whole lists of stats, or ten times the rules, or keep looking up things nonstop just to get the same stuff done as before.<br /> A little bit more complexity for the sake of realism is a-okay, especially if your players Feel More Badass (And/or more threatened by an enemy..) as a result. But use it to create atmosphere and fix immersion problems - not create new ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 08-29-2016, 02:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T11:41:34-07:00","id":959928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Innocent Flower</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/958881-a-good-system-for-armour-weapons?p=959805#post959805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also think that, well, having great strength should allow you an easier time in armour. No 'Well you get dex from celerity and that cancels out the dex penality' but, well. Strength should, but not completely, migitate the problems of having excess weight. Potence, whatever mages use, and maybe glabro if you find something fitting should all reduce penalties (with some hard armour keeping at least some penalty because of how rigid and in the way it is, rather than weight)</div> </div> </div> </div>While it might not be great from a design perspective, Stamina is really what should matter here. Armor isn't that heavy (~90 lbs is on the very heavy side of plate mail for example), and is spread out over the body in a design specifically to help distribute the load as effectively as possible on the human frame. However, that weight adds up in caloric expenditure over time. That's why people can do cartwheels in full plate mail; it isn't so heavy or so restrictive. But each one costs more energy than it would without all the extra weight. Since the game doesn't really have fights last long enough to have exhaustion be a thing, the best way to include this would be to have the armor penalty severity key off of Stamina rather than Strength. <br /> <br /> If we really wanted to model armor's drawback more &quot;realistically&quot; it would be best to move from the current Health Level system, to an Exhaustion/Fatigue/Stress track and with &quot;Wounds&quot; as individual status effects. Armor would be a trade off of improving defense against wounds, but make exhaustion management more difficult.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T12:49:01-07:00","id":959969,"title":"","content":"Yes, you do not have battles that last hours at a time, unlike in real life, where the majority of the time spent in battle is hiding from the other force or hunting down the other force.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}